WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.900
Hey, Yuma!

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:06.100
Where have you been wandering around all this time?

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:08.630
You really are <i>such</i> an idiot!

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.290
On top of that, you even got Kotori-<i>chan</i> involved!

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:13.530
A-... Akari-<i>san</i>, I...

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:16.900
I-It couldn't be helped. A mountain of things were going on...

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.730
This is Yuma we're talking about.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.570
I'm sure those things had to do with Dueling.

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:24.870
Right! It's a <i>huge</i> adventure with Dueling that-

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.210
 Aah, that hurts!

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.930
What huge adventure!? Watch your mouth, you little brat!

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:30.430
<i>Haru-san! Yuma!</i>

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:36.100
Gr-Granpa Rokujuro?!

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:40.720
<i>Here in the estate of Mr. Rokujuro's Duel Lodge lies</i>

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.790
<i>a stone statue dedicated to the military general, Souhachi Kiraku, of the Sengoku Era.</i>

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:47.500
<i>This is the discovery everyone's been talking about.</i>

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.470
<i>Afterwards, regarding Souhachi Kiraku's life...</i>

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.470
Where have I seen that face...?

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:52.790
<i>Mr. Rokujuro will tell us all about it!</i>

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:53.940
- Gilag?!
 - Gilag?!

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:57.410
What kind of person was Souhachi Kiraku?

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:00.510
He was very good at fighting.

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.720
He fought with the surrounding generals,

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.600
and donated all the treasures he obtained
 to the peasants in his territory.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.990
And yet he was an extremely frugal person himself.

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:13.020
He was indeed a legendary, reputable ruler of this land.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:13.890
<i>I see.</i>

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.850
Legendary?

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:17.260
Could this be...?

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.660
<i>This time, it seems you have discovered many things aside from the statue.</i>

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:25.170
<i>That's right. During this excavation... Here.</i>

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.100
<i>Tons of Kiraku-sama's treasures.</i>

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:31.830
Ah! That's Dad's coin!

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:33.580
That's right. There's no mistaking it.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:34.310
Huh?

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:38.000
On the map inside the airship that indicates the whereabouts of the Numbers,

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.780
the Duel Lodge was also shown.

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:42.560
Wha?! Say so sooner!

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:43.750
Gah, Yuma!

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:44.850
P-Please excuse us!

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:47.260
Ahh, Kotori-<i>chan</i>!

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:53.020
<i>Love suddenly fell down onto my field...</i>

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:54.930
What a pain in the ass.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:02:00.400
Why the hell do I have to waste time wandering around looking for Numbers?

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:04.510
Geez.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:11.810
<i>This Kiraku statue will be...</i>

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:11.810
This thing's... me?!

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:41.570
<i>Being best friends doesn't mean we always were</i>

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:44.620
<i>That's pretty much true</i>

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:52.080
<i>I found you during our serious battles</i>

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:55.630
<i>The other me inside myself</i>

00:02:55.630 --> 00:03:00.510
<i>Awakening from within the conflict</i>

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:06.850
<i>A turn for a chance! Seize it! Draw!</i>

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:10.060
<i>Duel! Dualism!</i>

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:12.940
<i>These cards are polished to fit each other</i>

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:17.570
<i>My fated opponent is my heart reflected through the mirror</i>

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:20.650
<i>And if we end up with a "tie" in the end,</i>

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:29.120
<i>when we fall, all covered with mud, we'll praise each other</i>

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:56.290
I-It really looks just like me.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:57.960
"Yuma Confused!? The Unreliable Account 
of Gilag the Raccoon Dog."

00:03:56.750 --> 00:04:00.590
Just what in the world is this thing?

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:02.680
Huh?

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:06.970
Th-This is a Number...!

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.100
Kiraku.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:08.510
Huh?

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:15.440
<i>I've been waiting for you, pon.</i>

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:18.190
I-I-It spoke!

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:23.740
If the protagonists of those legends really were the Barians... then Gilag really is...

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:26.910
But to think that guy used to be a such great general...

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:30.540
Look out!

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:32.540
Yuma!

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:40.670
Yuma!

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:44.760
Ow~!

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:45.970
You okay?

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:51.430
This...!

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:54.640
At last.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:00.530
I finally...got my freedom, pon!

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:02.990
You're... Gilag!

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:05.660
Pon?

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:07.530
Y-You are, right?

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:10.330
Hey, wait!

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.160
It's me, Yuma Tsukumo!

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:17.210
Then...it's a pleasure to meet you, pon.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.790
Please excuse me, pon.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:20.960
H-Hey...!

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:22.460
Wait a minute, dammit!

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:29.220
Gimme back... my body!

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.140
I-It spoke!

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:34.680
Why's the stone statue talking?!

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.940
I ain't a stone statue! I'm Gilag!

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.360
S-Say what?

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.190
Just what's going on here?

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:45.150
I got no clue, but I ended up trapped inside that statue!

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:47.530
The guy inside him... inside me...

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.450
...is the spirit of the Number!

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:51.870
The spirit of the Number?

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:56.580
Huh? Gilag's the statue and the statue's Gilag?!

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:58.330
That's way too annoying!

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:01.290
I know everything about you!

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:06.840
You've been secretly stealing sides from that girl's lunch box, haven't you?!

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:09.640
Don't underestimate the Barian's data network!

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:14.390
No wonder I always felt I didn't eat enough during the day!

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:16.100
I-It wasn't me!

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.980
Anyway, how can that prove that it's you?!

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:21.480
Did you forget the Duel you had with me?!

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:25.190
You took my Giant Hand's Fatally Paralyzing Pressure Point Strike!

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.910
Th-Then you really are...!

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.950
That's right, pon. We've changed places, pon.

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:39.580
From now on, I'll live as Kiraku, pon!

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:42.080
Changed places?!

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:45.550
I was waiting for a long time inside that stone statue, pon.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.260
For the day I would obtain freedom.

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:53.510
And low and behold, Kiraku's aura appeared before me, pon!

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:57.930
So the legendary general named Souhachi Kiraku really is Gilag.

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:01.600
Hey, please! Win the Duel with him!

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:03.610
And get my body back!

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:05.780
Why must I do that for you?

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:08.950
That guy has a Number!

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:09.780
A Number?

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:11.030
Yuma.

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:15.700
If he really is holding a Number, then we have no choice.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:17.290
Yeah.

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:20.290
I don't really get any of this,

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:21.790
but I'll do it! Let's Duel!

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:27.760
Very interesting, pon! I won't forgive anyone who tries to steal my freedom, pon!

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:32.720
Okay, here we go! Duel Disk, set!

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:38.310
D-Gazer, set!

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:47.190
Duel!!

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:50.110
You can do it, Yuma!

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:51.990
You can do it, Yuma!

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:56.620
The first turn is mine, pon! My turn! Draw, pon!

00:07:56.620 --> 00:08:00.000
I Summon Pon-Poko the Raccoon Rascal!

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:04.040
Ah, so cute!

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:08.300
And I activate a Magic Card from my hand! Leaf Transformation!

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:13.470
It lets me Special Summon a Monster with Raccoon in its name from my hand!

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:16.050
Get out here, Tan-Tan the Raccoon Rascal!

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:17.970
It's on its way, Yuma!

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.310
I know.

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:23.600
I Overlay the Level Two Pon-Poko the Raccoon Rascal and Tan-Tan the Raccoon Rascal!

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:29.400
I use these two Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:31.030
Xyz Summon!

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:36.030
Show yourself, Number 64!

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:40.410
The sage that slays the chaos and the chaotic world!

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:44.620
Make the world change! Sandayu the Veteraccoon!

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:47.250
So that's the Number of these ruins...!

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:49.800
I activate Sandayu the Veteraccoon's effect!

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:53.880
Once per turn, I can remove one Overlay Unit

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:58.550
and I can Special Summon one Kagemusha Raccoon Token!

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:04.480
And its Attack Power is equal to the Monster on the field with the highest Attack Power!

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:05.730
What'd you say?!

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:10.230
When I have a Kagemusha Raccoon Token on my field,

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:13.900
Sandayu the Veteraccoon cannot be targeted for an attack, pon!

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:16.950
But its Attack Power is only 1000!

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:19.160
I'm not scared of no Kagemusha!

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:22.290
Don't underestimate the shadows, pon. Shadows.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.250
I will now end my turn, pon!

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:26.250
Shadows...?

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:27.120
Yuma.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:28.630
R-Right!

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:31.630
My turn! Draw!

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:34.420
Yes, I got it!

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:35.670
Yuma!

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:36.590
Yeah!

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:40.350
I set one card face-down!

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:43.220
<i>That card...</i>

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:50.820
What the?!

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:52.320
Pon!

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:58.610
Yuma?

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:05.750
Yuma? Whiskers?

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:10.500
Huh? Why do I see myself?

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:15.300
Huh? Wha?! You...!

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:17.470
Why are you able to see my cards?!

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:22.600
I see. That set card...

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:29.810
When I don't have a Monster on my field,

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:33.650
I can Special Summon Toy Knight from my hand, pon!

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:35.940
Pon?

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:37.780
Astral! Kotori!

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:40.910
It's me! I'm over here!

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:42.740
Huh? What're you saying?

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:45.580
I'm saying I'm Yuma!

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:46.370
Eh?

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:51.250
I'm sorry! I was the one who stole from your lunch box!

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:53.250
I-Is that you, Yuma?

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.000
Drat! He went and did it!

00:10:55.590 --> 00:10:58.170
He... changed places with Yuma?!

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:02.090
You impostor jerk!

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:06.060
I am now the master of this body, pon.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:09.940
That's why I know what that set card is...

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:13.020
It's meant for the Summoning of this card!

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:16.280
When I have a Magic or Trap Card on my field,

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:19.240
I can Special Summon Dododo Witch, pon!

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.450
Now there's two Level Four Monsters.

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:28.830
I release Toy Knight and Dododo Witch!

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:30.660
Release them?!

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:33.420
...and then I Advance Summon the 3000 Defense Power...

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:36.840
...Dododo Gasser in Attack Position, pon!

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:43.890
What?!

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:45.350
It's got zero Attack Points!

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:47.720
Normally we would have played Hope!

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:52.230
Then I activate the Magic Card, Resurrection of the Dead!

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:55.270
I bring Toy Knight back from the Graveyard!

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:58.320
Then I activate the Magic Card, Guard Plus!

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:00.360
By releasing one Monster,

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:02.610
it increases the Defense Power of one Monster on my field

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:06.660
equal to the amount of the released Monster's Attack Points!

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:08.490
I release Toy Knight!

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:12.290
And I increase Dododo Gasser's Defense Power by 200!

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:15.130
There's no point if it's in Attack Mode!

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:21.130
Then I attack with the zero Attack Power Dododo Gasser!

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:24.930
Shit...! But you're going to take the pain!

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:26.760
Don't be so sure of that, pon!

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:29.270
Wha?

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:41.280
Eh?! No way!

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:43.320
Darn!

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:48.990
I like Kiraku better after all, pon!

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:50.620
Drat...!

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:56.080
Hey, Impostor Gilag! Why are you doing all of this?!

00:12:56.500 --> 00:13:01.170
I used to be Souhachi Kiraku's... Kagemusha, pon.

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:02.970
Kagemusha?
 ["Shadow Warrior"]

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:06.720
What "legend", pon? "Renowned ruler", pon?!

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:09.310
I am the one who won on the battlefield, pon!

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:12.770
That legend exists because of me, pon!

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:17.980
It's because of everything I did as a raccoon dog, changing into Souhachi Kiraku, pon!

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:19.980
R-Raccoon dog?!

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:26.570
You...used to be a raccoon dog?!

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:27.910
He does say "pon"...

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:29.120
And he uses a Raccoon Deck...

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:31.540
So the Number Spirit is a raccoon dog?

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:35.040
My encounter with Kiraku happened on the battlefield, pon.

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:39.590
As a raccoon dog, I was lost on the intense battlefield.

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:41.960
And he was the one who saved me, pon.

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:47.180
In order to repay his kindness, I shape shifted into Kiraku,

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:49.300
and I became his Kagemusha.

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:52.470
I fought in his place, pon.

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:56.270
I was strong. I was a genius.

00:13:56.270 --> 00:14:00.480
I made the country stronger, pon.
 Strong enough to conquer all, pon.

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:08.610
Even so, Kiraku ended up firing me, pon!

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:10.450
He was jealous of my strength, pon!

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:15.200
Afterward, my stupid master Kiraku ended up losing on the battlefield and dying, pon.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:18.710
if I was out there, I'd have definitely won the battle, pon!

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:22.380
Serves him right, pon!

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:27.090
Soon after, I died myself as a raccoon dog.

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:30.760
But before I realized it, my soul had

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:34.220
been trapped inside that Kiraku statue, pon.

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:36.810
I had become the Kagemusha of a dead man, pon!

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:40.190
I'm tired of being a shadow!

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:42.230
I want to become real, pon!

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:47.030
Shut up! Yuma, hurry and defeat him and get my body back!

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:52.910
Yuma, since he doesn't have Gilag's soul right now, we can defeat him and obtain the Number.

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:54.830
I know, but...

00:14:55.740 --> 00:15:01.040
Hey, raccoon dog, you're right about that Gilag jerk being a despicable bastard.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:04.750
He's also stingy and an annoying jerk!

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:07.130
That was uncalled for, you asshole!

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:09.220
But... But, you see...

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:12.470
I just can't bring myself to hate him.

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:13.260
Yuma...

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:18.480
I don't really care, pon! I already hate him more than enough, pon!

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:20.940
My turn! Draw, pon!

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:25.150
I activate Sandayu the Veteraccoon's effect, pon!

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:28.190
By detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:31.360
I can Special Summon one Kagemusha Raccoon Token, pon!

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:35.450
I attack directly with Sandayu the Veteraccoon, pon!

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:45.250
Once again! I attack directly with Kagemusha Raccoon Token, pon!

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:57.310
Alright, with the final shadow, I deliver the final blow with the Kagemusha Raccoon Token, pon!

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:02.480
Don't be so sure, pon!

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:03.270
Huh?!

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:06.230
<i>The set card... No, that card...</i>

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:08.900
<i>It's the card he set to Summon Dododo Witch.</i>

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:12.860
I will not fear the shadows, pon!

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:15.950
I Direct Attack with the Kagemusha Raccoon Token!

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:19.080
Heck yeah! Trap, activate!

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:20.950
Burst Reverse!

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:22.250
What's that, pon?!

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:23.750
I pay half my Life,

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:27.630
and Special Summon one Monster from my Graveyard in face-down Defense Position!

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:30.300
I set Dododo Gasser!

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:32.840
Dododo Gasser?!

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:37.760
Kagemusha Raccoon Token, stop the battle!

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:45.480
<i>But I still have this card, pon...</i>

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:49.900
I set one card face-down and end my turn, pon!

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:51.900
I will definitely defeat you, pon!

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:54.200
After you abandoned me,

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:57.120
it's time for you to become <i>my</i> Kagemusha, pon!

00:16:58.030 --> 00:17:01.330
And we can't afford to lose either!

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:02.290
Yuma!

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:06.040
My turn! Draw!

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:12.920
I will now Flip Summon Dododo Gasser!

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:20.180
Zero Attack Points, in Attack Mode?!

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:25.020
No, when it's successfully Flip Summoned, Dododo Gasser's Attack Power is...

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:28.150
...the same as the difference between our Life!

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:31.780
The difference between our Life is 3500!

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:37.160
So Dododo Gasser's Attack Power increases by 3500 points!

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:41.080
Dododo Gasser still has another Reverse Effect left!

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:44.080
He can destroy two Monsters on my opponent's field!

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:49.790
My shadows...!

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:53.210
I attack Sandayu the Veteraccoon with Dododo Gasser!

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:07.140
Po...

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:11.480
Now's the time, pon! Trap, activate! Senjyojiki Flip!

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:15.240
When a Raccoon Monster battles,

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:19.700
it destroys one of the opponent's Monsters
 and the opposing player takes

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:21.370
damage equal to its Attack Power!

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:23.950
Now I've won, pon!

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:26.330
No you don't!

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.670
Wh-What is it, pon?! That card?!

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:31.750
When the opponent activates a Trap Card,

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:33.960
by sending Chauchauchan to the Graveyard,

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:38.630
I can use the opponent's activated Trap Card as my own Trap Card!

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:43.060
Meaning I can use the effect of Senjyojiki Flip!

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:45.520
N-No way!

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:50.980
Destroy Sandayu the Veteraccoon!

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:56.740
And then you take Destroy Sandayu the Veteraccoon's Attack Power, 1000, as damage!

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:01.870
I'm gonna bring it to ya!

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:04.580
Dododo Gasser, Direct Attack!

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:06.500
Triple Bamboo Hat Strom!

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:11.710
Why did I...?!

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:17.340
Ponta!

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:32.770
I'm...not a shadow, pon.

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:35.020
I'm... I'm...

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:36.530
You're Ponta.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:40.070
Master...?

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:43.700
How nostalgic, Ponta.

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:46.370
Is this the great Kiraku?

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:49.160
Then Gilag really is Kiraku...

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:52.120
Why did you abandon me, pon?

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:55.590
We were going to lose that battle from the very beginning.

00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:57.500
Th-That isn't true!

00:19:57.500 --> 00:19:59.720
if I had been there fighting...

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:00.470
No.

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:06.810
The vassals who didn't receive the wealth
 I gave to the peasants rebelled.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:10.850
Before I realized it, things had gotten out of hand.

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:16.230
I was thinking that, at the very least, I wanted you to escape, Ponta.

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:20.530
That can't be! I... don't like that, pon!

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:24.570
I wanted you to tell me that we'd fight together!

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:25.870
So we could have been together...!

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:31.500
I... I'm... I'm...

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:35.080
Ponta...

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:40.880
I'll...entrust you guys with the Number, pon.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:43.380
It's the least I can do to pay you back...

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:44.840
Astral...

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:45.590
Yeah.

00:20:57.560 --> 00:20:58.820
<i>Kiraku-sama.</i>

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:05.820
Like hell that's true!

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:19.880
S-Stop it...!

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:31.970
I can't believe you were completely deceived by my made up story.

00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:34.770
You're all idiots!

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:35.850
You...!

00:21:35.980 --> 00:21:41.690
Yuma Tsukumo! Next time we meet, I swear to defeat you!

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:46.660
Gilag...! You...!

00:21:56.750 --> 00:22:01.210
How did I know that story...?

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:03.210
Pon!

00:22:21.230 --> 00:22:23.730
<i>Is it the world that's boring?</i>

00:22:23.730 --> 00:22:26.280
<i>Or maybe you're the one who's not gettin' serious?</i>

00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:27.490
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:28.910
<i>Do I understand?</i>

00:22:29.110 --> 00:22:31.780
<i>Already got my answers</i>

00:22:31.830 --> 00:22:34.290
<i>Once you start movin', you ain't stoppin'</i>

00:22:34.290 --> 00:22:36.830
<i>I go on thinkin' even while losin'.</i>

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:37.910
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:37.910 --> 00:22:38.960
<i>I understand!</i>

00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:42.340
<i>Our formula for reversal's already gathered</i>

00:22:42.340 --> 00:22:44.670
<i>You afraid it ain't comin' true?</i>

00:22:44.670 --> 00:22:47.800
<i>I gotta 'least give it a try</i>

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:50.010
<i>Ain't no problem if they say I'm borin'</i>

00:22:50.010 --> 00:22:53.010
<i>True failure's when we stop movin'</i>

00:22:53.180 --> 00:22:54.970
<i>Come on! Ga, ga, ga, guys & dolls</i>

00:22:54.970 --> 00:22:56.350
<i>Go, go, go, go my way</i>

00:22:56.350 --> 00:22:58.230
<i>Oh, oh, oh, over ray</i>

00:22:58.520 --> 00:23:02.520
<i>Door's always open for you</i>

00:23:02.690 --> 00:23:07.610
<i>Bring your power forth and go way, go way</i>

00:23:07.610 --> 00:23:08.860
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:08.860 --> 00:23:12.870
<i>And tears are no way, no way</i>

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:18.250
<i>With all my strength, pave way, go way</i>

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:19.460
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:19.460 --> 00:23:23.590
<i>Got all the courage here</i>

00:23:23.590 --> 00:23:25.750
<i>You ought to understand!</i>

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:27.960
<i>Go way, go way</i>

00:23:40.140 --> 00:23:42.230
We continue our search for ruins containing Numbers.

00:23:42.730 --> 00:23:45.690
Our next destination is inside an ocean amidst a terrible storm!

00:23:46.070 --> 00:23:49.280
After being called mysteriously, Rio falls into the ocean.

00:23:49.860 --> 00:23:53.950
And while searching for her, a giant labyrinth appears before us.

00:23:53.950 --> 00:23:55.620
Rio-<i>san</i>'s inside the ocean!

00:23:55.620 --> 00:23:59.370
It would appear that common sense does not apply to this maze.

00:23:59.660 --> 00:24:01.250
Shark disappeared!

00:24:01.250 --> 00:24:03.790
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II!

00:24:03.790 --> 00:24:07.000
"Invitation to the Bottom of the Ocean!
 Shark's Dream-like Memory."

00:24:07.300 --> 00:24:08.960
Is there really a Number here?
